{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"aragonite-bleached-vipersquid","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nDiscovered while proving `abusive-pebbly-sakimonkey` (e339-9709-15fe-419a). Independent of\nthat ticket's FIT divergence: under `reconciler.rich_text_cutover = \"cloud\"` (this project's\nsetting, `rebar.toml:87`) the outbound comment differ decodes the two sides of its\nbody-equality key with DIFFERENT decoders, so a markdown comment WELL WITHIN the length limit\nnever matches its own landed body.\n\n- **Local side** — `_diff_comments` computes `codec.normalize_outbound(...)`. In rich mode\n  `AdfCodec.normalize_outbound` is a markdown round trip, which ESCAPES markdown-active\n  characters and rewrites autolinks.\n- **Jira side** — `_normalize_comment_body` calls `inbound_mapper.normalize_rich_text`\n  (`inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text` -> `adf_to_text`), which does NOT escape.\n\n## Runtime evidence\n\nDriving the real `AdfCodec(rich=True)` and `_JiraInbound` on current main\n(worktree `fix-sakimonkey-dedupkey`), with an in-limit markdown body:\n\n```\nlocal key : '# Head\\n\\nSome *bold* text and a [link](<http://x>) plus `code`.\\n\\n- a\\n- b'\nlanded key: '# Head\\n\\nSome *bold* text and a [link](http://x) plus `code`.\\n\\n- a\\n- b'\nEQUAL?    : False\n```\n\nThe same asymmetry escapes the truncation notice: the local key carries\n`\\[truncated by reconciler\\]` where the landed body carries `[truncated by reconciler]`.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nBody equality is the SECONDARY dedup layer guarding a lost comment-id map write (the crash\nwindow between `add_comment` and `record_comment_id`). With the cutover ON it is inert for\nevery markdown-formatted comment, not just over-length ones — a strictly wider blast radius\nthan the fit divergence. `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker`'s commit message names this symptom\n(\"richly formatted comments never matched and were re-posted forever\") but repaired the\nPRIMARY id skip, not this decode asymmetry.\n\nThis is NOT fixed by `abusive-pebbly-sakimonkey`, which makes the two paths apply the identical\nFIT. Verified: after that fix the in-limit markdown case still diverges, for this reason.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The differ's two comparison keys are produced by the same decode under every\n      `rich_text_cutover` setting.\n- [ ] A test drives an in-limit markdown comment through the differ with the cutover ON and\n      asserts no duplicate mutation is emitted (RED on current code).","id":"17c3-2f6e-a5e0-438c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Cloud comment dedup key is markdown-escaped on one side only"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787305651742009001,"uuid":"63df06b6-cdbe-4743-91b8-8f974c9fa209"}